IMPORT prelude

-- Protection from Harassment Act 2014 (Singapore) -- Part 2, the offences.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 17 August 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PHA2014.txt.
-- The deposit carries the amendments made by Act 23 of 2025 with effect from
-- 29 June 2026, which rewrote the harm formula in ss 3, 4 and 7 to add
-- "humiliation" and added the online-activity limbs to s 7(3).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED in this file: s 9 (community order -- a power), and everything
-- from Division 2 of Part 3 onwards (the false-statement orders in ss 15 to
-- 16BB, Part 3A on the Protection from Harassment Court, and Part 4). See
-- NOTES.md on why the false-statement regime was left out.

§ `Protection from Harassment Act 2014 -- Part 2`

§§ `2 -- the terms the offences are built from`

-- s 2(1): "'communication' means any words, image (moving or otherwise),
-- message, expression, symbol or other representation that can be seen, heard
-- or otherwise perceived by any person, or any combination of these".
--
-- s 2(1): "'identity information' means any information that, whether on its own
-- or with other information, identifies or purports to identify an individual",
-- including the individual's name, residential address, email address, telephone
-- number, date of birth, NRIC number, passport number, signature or password;
-- any photograph or video recording of the individual; and any information about
-- the individual's family, employment or education.
--
-- s 2(1): "'related person', in relation to a person, means another person about
-- whose safety or wellbeing the firstmentioned person would reasonably be
-- expected to be seriously concerned".
--
-- The five adjectives that qualify words, behaviour and communications are not
-- the same in every section. ss 3, 4 and 6 use all five; s 5(1) uses only the
-- first three. This is carried as a record of the five rather than a single
-- flag, because the difference decides cases.
DECLARE Quality HAS
    `threatening` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abusive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `insulting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sexual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `indecent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ss 3(1)(a) and (b), 4(1)(a) and (b), 6(1)(a) and (b).
GIVEN `the quality` IS A Quality
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the words or communication are of a quality sections 3, 4 and 6 name` IF
        `the quality`'s `threatening`
    OR  `the quality`'s `abusive`
    OR  `the quality`'s `insulting`
    OR  `the quality`'s `sexual`
    OR  `the quality`'s `indecent`

-- s 5(1): "any threatening, abusive or insulting words or behaviour". Sexual and
-- indecent are not there, and s 5 is the violence section, so nothing is lost
-- except that the section cannot be reached by indecency alone.
GIVEN `the quality` IS A Quality
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the words or communication are of a quality section 5(1) names` IF
        `the quality`'s `threatening`
    OR  `the quality`'s `abusive`
    OR  `the quality`'s `insulting`

§§ `3 -- intentionally causing harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`

-- s 3(1): an individual or entity must not, "WITH INTENT to cause harassment,
-- alarm, distress or humiliation to another person (called in this section the
-- target person), by any means --
--   (a) use any threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent words or
--       behaviour;
--   (b) make any threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent
--       communication; or
--   (c) PUBLISH ANY IDENTITY INFORMATION of the target person or a related
--       person of the target person,
-- and AS A RESULT causing the target person OR ANY OTHER PERSON (each called in
-- this section the victim) harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation."
--
-- Three elements: the intent, one of the three kinds of conduct, and a result.
-- The result need not fall on the person the intent was aimed at -- the section
-- names "the target person or any other person" as the victim. Illustration (c)
-- is exactly that case: Y never saw the posts and was harassed by the strangers
-- who did.
--
-- s 3(3): "it is a defence for the accused to prove that the accused's conduct
-- was reasonable." Note the framing -- "in any proceedings FOR AN OFFENCE under
-- subsection (2)". See pha-civil.l4 on what that does to the statutory tort.
DECLARE Section3Facts HAS
    `intent to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation to the target person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS A Quality
    `used words or behaviour, or made a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published identity information of the target person or a related person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result the target person was caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result some other person was caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section3Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 3(1) conduct is made out` IF
         (    `the facts`'s `used words or behaviour, or made a communication`
          AND `the words or communication are of a quality sections 3, 4 and 6 name` (`the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`))
    OR  `the facts`'s `published identity information of the target person or a related person`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section3Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(1) is contravened` IF
        `the facts`'s `intent to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation to the target person`
    AND `a limb of section 3(1) conduct is made out` `the facts`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `as a result the target person was caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
         OR  `the facts`'s `as a result some other person was caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section3Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 3(2) is committed` IF
        `section 3(1) is contravened` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the conduct was reasonable`

§§ `4 -- harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation without intent`

-- s 4(1): an individual or entity must not by any means --
--   (a) use any threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent words or
--       behaviour;
--   (b) make any threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent
--       communication,
-- "which is heard, seen or otherwise perceived by any person (called in this
-- section the victim) LIKELY TO BE CAUSED harassment, alarm, distress or
-- humiliation."
--
-- There is no intent requirement and no requirement that anyone was actually
-- harassed -- only that a person who perceived it was likely to be caused the
-- harm.
--
-- AND THERE IS NO LIMB (c). s 3 has a third limb for publishing identity
-- information; s 4 does not. Identity information is not, on its own,
-- threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent -- a home address is none
-- of those -- which is precisely why s 3 needed a separate limb for it. The
-- consequence is recorded in the cases file and in NOTES.md.
--
-- s 4(1A): an individual or entity "DOES NOT CONTRAVENE subsection (1) where the
-- sexual or indecent words or behaviour, or the sexual or indecent communication
-- (as the case may be), has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine,
-- education or art." The Explanation adds that a purpose related to art is one
-- "which a reasonable person would regard as art."
--
-- Two things about s 4(1A). It is drafted as a NON-CONTRAVENTION, not as a
-- defence -- unlike s 4(3). And it reaches only the sexual and indecent limbs: a
-- threatening or abusive communication with a legitimate educational purpose is
-- outside it and must rely on s 4(3)(b) instead.
--
-- s 4(3): it is a defence to the OFFENCE to prove (a) no reason to believe the
-- words would be perceived by the victim, or (b) that the conduct was
-- reasonable.
DECLARE Section4Facts HAS
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS A Quality
    `used words or behaviour, or made a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published identity information of the victim or a related person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `heard, seen or otherwise perceived by a person likely to be caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1A) bites only where the quality relied on is the sexual or indecent one.
-- If the conduct is also threatening, abusive or insulting, the subsection does
-- not reach it.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section4Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(1A) takes the conduct outside subsection (1)` IF
        `the facts`'s `has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`'s `sexual`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`'s `indecent`)
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`'s `threatening`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`'s `abusive`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`'s `insulting`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section4Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(1) is contravened` IF
        `the facts`'s `used words or behaviour, or made a communication`
    AND `the words or communication are of a quality sections 3, 4 and 6 name` (`the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`)
    AND `the facts`'s `heard, seen or otherwise perceived by a person likely to be caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND NOT `section 4(1A) takes the conduct outside subsection (1)` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section4Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 4(2) is committed` IF
        `section 4(1) is contravened` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the conduct was reasonable`

§§ `5 -- fear, provocation or facilitation of violence`

-- s 5(1): must not use towards another person any threatening, abusive or
-- insulting words or behaviour, or make such a communication to another person,
-- either --
--   (a) with the intent (i) to cause the victim to believe that unlawful
--       violence will be used by any person against the victim or any other
--       person, or (ii) to provoke the use of unlawful violence by the victim or
--       another person against any other person; or
--   (b) whereby (i) the victim is LIKELY to believe such violence will be used,
--       or (ii) it is LIKELY that such violence will be provoked.
--
-- s 5(1A): must not publish any identity information of another person or a
-- related person, either (a) with the intent to cause belief in unlawful
-- violence or TO FACILITATE its use, or (b) KNOWING OR HAVING REASONABLE CAUSE
-- TO BELIEVE that it is likely to do either.
--
-- So s 5 does have an identity-information limb, added by Act 17 of 2019, and
-- its fault requirement in (1A)(b) is knowledge or reasonable cause to believe
-- -- lower than intent but not the bare likelihood that s 5(1)(b) uses.
--
-- s 5(3): defences -- (a) for a contravention of SUBSECTION (1)(b) ONLY, no
-- reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim; and (b) reasonable
-- conduct. Note that (a) is confined to (1)(b): it is not available to an
-- accused who had the intent under (1)(a), which makes sense, nor to one who
-- published identity information under (1A).
DECLARE Section5Facts HAS
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS A Quality
    `used words or behaviour towards another person, or made a communication to them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published identity information of the victim or a related person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intent to cause the victim to believe unlawful violence will be used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intent to provoke the use of unlawful violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intent to facilitate the use of unlawful violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is likely to believe such violence will be used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely that such violence will be provoked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it likely to cause such belief or facilitate such violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(1)(a) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `used words or behaviour towards another person, or made a communication to them`
    AND `the words or communication are of a quality section 5(1) names` (`the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `intent to cause the victim to believe unlawful violence will be used`
         OR  `the facts`'s `intent to provoke the use of unlawful violence`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(1)(b) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `used words or behaviour towards another person, or made a communication to them`
    AND `the words or communication are of a quality section 5(1) names` (`the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the victim is likely to believe such violence will be used`
         OR  `the facts`'s `it is likely that such violence will be provoked`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(1A) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `published identity information of the victim or a related person`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `intent to cause the victim to believe unlawful violence will be used`
         OR  `the facts`'s `intent to facilitate the use of unlawful violence`
         OR  `the facts`'s `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it likely to cause such belief or facilitate such violence`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 is contravened` IF
        `section 5(1)(a) is made out` `the facts`
    OR  `section 5(1)(b) is made out` `the facts`
    OR  `section 5(1A) is made out` `the facts`

-- The s 5(3)(a) defence is confined to a contravention of subsection (1)(b).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 5(3)(a) defence is available` IF
        `the facts`'s `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim`
    AND `section 5(1)(b) is made out` `the facts`
    AND NOT `section 5(1)(a) is made out` `the facts`
    AND NOT `section 5(1A) is made out` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section5Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 5(2) is committed` IF
        `section 5 is contravened` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the section 5(3)(a) defence is available` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the conduct was reasonable`

§§ `6 -- public servants and public service workers`

-- s 6(1): conduct of the five qualities "towards or to a public servant or public
-- service worker ... IN RELATION TO THE EXECUTION OF THE DUTY of the public
-- servant or public service worker" is an offence. s 6(1A) adds a publication
-- limb for identity information.
--
-- s 6(2): "NO OFFENCE IS COMMITTED under this section unless the accused knows or
-- ought reasonably to know that the victim was acting in the victim's capacity
-- as a public servant or public service worker."
--
-- s 6(3): a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or
-- both.
-- s 6(4): defences -- (a) for subsection (1), no reason to believe it would be
-- perceived by the victim; (b) for either subsection, reasonable conduct.
--
-- s 6 is the orphan of this Act. It is in s 12 (protection order) and in s 8
-- (subsequent conviction), and it is in NEITHER s 11 (the statutory tort) NOR
-- s 8A and s 8B (the vulnerable-person and intimate-relationship enhancements).
-- See pha-civil.l4 and NOTES.md.
DECLARE Section6Facts HAS
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS A Quality
    `used words or behaviour towards the victim, or made a communication to them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published identity information of the victim or a related person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is a public servant or public service worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct was in relation to the execution of the victim's duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section6Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6(1) conduct is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `used words or behaviour towards the victim, or made a communication to them`
    AND `the words or communication are of a quality sections 3, 4 and 6 name` (`the facts`'s `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication`)
    AND `the facts`'s `the victim is a public servant or public service worker`
    AND `the facts`'s `the conduct was in relation to the execution of the victim's duty`

-- s 6(2) is not a defence: it is a condition on the commission of the offence,
-- so the absence of knowledge means no offence at all rather than an answer to
-- one.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section6Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6 is committed` IF
        `section 6(1) conduct is made out` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was acting in that capacity`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the conduct was reasonable`

§§ `7 -- unlawful stalking`

-- s 7(1): an individual or entity must not unlawfully stalk another person.
--
-- s 7(2): "SUBJECT TO SUBSECTION (7)", the accused unlawfully stalks the victim
-- if the accused engages in a course of conduct which --
--   (a) involves acts or omissions associated with stalking;
--   (b) causes harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation to the victim; and
--   (c) the accused (i) INTENDS to cause it, or (ii) KNOWS OR OUGHT REASONABLY
--       TO KNOW is likely to cause it.
--
-- Note the opening words. The subsection that defines unlawful stalking is
-- expressed to be subject to the defences in s 7(7), so for s 7 -- unlike
-- ss 3, 4, 5 and 6 -- the defences bear on whether the conduct is unlawful
-- stalking at all, and therefore on whether s 7(1) was contravened. The
-- difference matters to the statutory tort; see pha-civil.l4.
--
-- s 7(4): the accused "ought reasonably to know" if "a reasonable person in
-- possession of the same information would think that the course of conduct is
-- likely to have that effect."
--
-- s 7(10): "'course of conduct' means conduct --
--   (a) on ONE occasion, if (i) the conduct is PROTRACTED; or (ii) the accused
--       has a PREVIOUS CONVICTION under this section in respect of the same
--       victim; or
--   (b) on 2 OR MORE occasions in any other case."
--
-- So a single occasion will do if it is protracted, and a single non-protracted
-- occasion will do against a victim the accused has already been convicted of
-- stalking. The second limb makes the course-of-conduct threshold turn on the
-- accused's record rather than on the conduct.
DECLARE StalkingFacts HAS
    `the number of occasions` IS A NUMBER
    `the conduct is protracted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a previous conviction under section 7 in respect of the same victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves acts or omissions associated with stalking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `causes harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation to the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable person with the same information would think it likely to have that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course of conduct was reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pursued under any written law or rule of law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully done under a power for preventing or detecting crime` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done on behalf of the Government and necessary for national security, defence or international relations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a ministerial certificate under section 7(8) has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a course of conduct within section 7(10)` IF
        `the facts`'s `the number of occasions` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `the number of occasions` AT LEAST 1
         AND (    `the facts`'s `the conduct is protracted`
              OR  `the facts`'s `a previous conviction under section 7 in respect of the same victim`))

-- s 7(4): the objective limb of s 7(2)(c)(ii).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fault element in section 7(2)(c) is satisfied` IF
        `the facts`'s `intends to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    OR  `the facts`'s `a reasonable person with the same information would think it likely to have that effect`

-- s 7(8): the certificate is "CONCLUSIVE EVIDENCE that the act falls within that
-- paragraph", so where it has issued the limb is established whatever the facts.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the national security limb of section 7(7)(d) is established` IF
        `the facts`'s `a ministerial certificate under section 7(8) has been issued`
    OR  `the facts`'s `done on behalf of the Government and necessary for national security, defence or international relations`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defence in section 7(7) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `the course of conduct was reasonable in all the circumstances`
    OR  `the facts`'s `pursued under any written law or rule of law`
    OR  `the facts`'s `lawfully done under a power for preventing or detecting crime`
    OR  `the national security limb of section 7(7)(d) is established` `the facts`

-- s 7(2), read with its opening words.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused unlawfully stalks the victim` IF
        `there is a course of conduct within section 7(10)` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `involves acts or omissions associated with stalking`
    AND `the facts`'s `causes harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation to the victim`
    AND `the fault element in section 7(2)(c) is satisfied` `the facts`
    AND NOT `a defence in section 7(7) is made out` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(1) is contravened` IF
    `the accused unlawfully stalks the victim` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A StalkingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 7(6) is committed` IF
    `section 7(1) is contravened` `the facts`

§§ `8, 8A, 8B and 8C -- the enhanced penalties`

-- The maxima, and the three ways they move.
--
-- s 3(2): $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 4(2): a fine not exceeding $5,000 -- AND NOTHING ELSE. s 4 is the only
--   offence in Part 2 that carries no imprisonment on a first conviction.
-- s 5(2): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 6(3): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 7(6): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 10(1): $5,000 or 6 months or both.
--
-- s 8(1): on a subsequent conviction -- $10,000 and, for s 3, 12 months; for
--   s 4, 6 MONTHS; for ss 5, 6 and 7, 2 years.
-- s 8(2): on a subsequent conviction under s 10 -- $10,000 or 12 months or both.
--
-- s 8A(2): where the victim is a vulnerable person and the offender knew or
--   ought reasonably to have known, the court may sentence "to punishment not
--   exceeding TWICE the maximum punishment" otherwise available -- but only for
--   an offence under s 3, 4, 5, 7 or 10, and only "where the enhanced penalty
--   under section 8 DOES NOT APPLY".
-- s 8A(2A): not where the offender proves the victim was capable of protecting
--   himself or herself in the same manner as an ordinary person.
-- s 8B(2): the same doubling for a victim who was or is in an intimate
--   relationship with the offender, on the same sections and with the same
--   exclusion of s 8.
-- s 8B(4): not where the offender proves the relationship did not adversely
--   affect the victim's ability to protect themselves.
-- s 8C: where both s 8A and s 8B apply, "the punishment for that offence shall
--   not be enhanced by the application of MORE THAN ONE section."
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `the maximum fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE OffenceSection IS ONE OF
    `section 3`
    `section 4`
    `section 5`
    `section 6`
    `section 7`
    `section 10`

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `the penalty on a first conviction` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 3`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 6
    WHEN `section 4`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 0
    WHEN `section 5`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 12
    WHEN `section 6`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 12
    WHEN `section 7`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 12
    OTHERWISE              Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 6

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `the penalty under section 8 on a subsequent conviction` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 3`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 12
    WHEN `section 4`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 6
    WHEN `section 5`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24
    WHEN `section 6`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24
    WHEN `section 7`  THEN Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 24
    OTHERWISE              Penalty WITH `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000, `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 12

GIVEN `the penalty` IS A Penalty
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `twice` IS
    Penalty WITH
        `the maximum fine in dollars` IS 2 TIMES `the penalty`'s `the maximum fine in dollars`
        `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS 2 TIMES `the penalty`'s `the maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 8A and s 8B list ss 3, 4, 5, 7 and 10. s 6 is not among them.
GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 8A and 8B reach this offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 6` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE SentencingFacts HAS
    `a subsequent conviction within section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is a vulnerable person and the offender knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim was capable of protecting himself or herself as an ordinary person would` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim was or is in an intimate relationship with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relationship did not adversely affect the victim's ability to protect themselves` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection, `the facts` IS A SentencingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8A applies` IF
        `sections 8A and 8B reach this offence` `the section`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `a subsequent conviction within section 8`
    AND `the facts`'s `the victim is a vulnerable person and the offender knew or ought to have known`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the victim was capable of protecting himself or herself as an ordinary person would`

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection, `the facts` IS A SentencingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8B applies` IF
        `sections 8A and 8B reach this offence` `the section`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `a subsequent conviction within section 8`
    AND `the facts`'s `the victim was or is in an intimate relationship with the offender`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the relationship did not adversely affect the victim's ability to protect themselves`

-- s 8C: one doubling at most, whichever of s 8A and s 8B applies.
GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection, `the facts` IS A SentencingFacts
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `the maximum punishment` IS
    IF   `the facts`'s `a subsequent conviction within section 8`
    THEN `the penalty under section 8 on a subsequent conviction` `the section`
    ELSE IF   `section 8A applies` `the section` `the facts`
                  OR `section 8B applies` `the section` `the facts`
         THEN `twice` (`the penalty on a first conviction` `the section`)
         ELSE `the penalty on a first conviction` `the section`

§§ `10 -- contravention of a protection order`

-- s 10(1): an individual or entity "that, WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE, fails to
-- comply with an order made under -- (a) section 12(2) or (2E); or (b) section
-- 13(1) or (1B)" is guilty of an offence, with the exception of the counselling
-- or mediation referral in s 12(2B)(c).
--
-- So the one thing a protection order can require that is NOT backed by this
-- offence is attendance at counselling or mediation.
--
-- s 10(1A): the accused "is PRESUMED, until the contrary is proved, to have
-- knowledge of the terms of an order made under this Act at and after the time
-- when the order takes effect."
-- s 10(3) and (4): a non-compliance punished under s 10(1) is not punishable as
-- contempt, and one punished as contempt cannot be convicted under s 10(1).
-- Election, not accumulation.
DECLARE NonComplianceFacts HAS
    `failed to comply with an order under section 12(2), 12(2E), 13(1) or 13(1B)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what was not complied with is the counselling or mediation referral under section 12(2B)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved absence of knowledge of the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order had taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the non-compliance has been punished as a contempt of court` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 10(1A) puts the burden on the accused, so knowledge is taken as present
-- unless disproved.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A NonComplianceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is taken to know the terms of the order` IF
        `the facts`'s `the order had taken effect`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `proved absence of knowledge of the terms of the order`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A NonComplianceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10(1) is committed` IF
        `the facts`'s `failed to comply with an order under section 12(2), 12(2E), 13(1) or 13(1B)`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `what was not complied with is the counselling or mediation referral under section 12(2B)(c)`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `had a reasonable excuse`
    AND `the accused is taken to know the terms of the order` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the non-compliance has been punished as a contempt of court`
